<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Raymond FitzGerald</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Raymond le Gros</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Raymond FitzGerald, called le Gros, was a Cambro-Norman knight who took part in the English invasion of Ireland. Sent ahead by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/richard-de-clare-2nd-earl-of-pembroke">Strongbow</a> in 1170, he landed at Baginbun and defeated a force from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/waterford">Waterford</a>, and he joined Strongbow in storming the town that August. He married Strongbow's sister Basilia and served as one of the leading commanders of the Anglo-Norman settlers in Leinster.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/raymond-fitzgerald.jpg" alt="Raymond FitzGerald" width="320" height="657" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown artist of the 13th century · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:National_Library_of_Ireland_MS_700_f77v_Raymond_de_Gros.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
